# README - Stack Operations

## Aim
This folder contains stack-related programs that demonstrate the basic stack operations using different implementations.

---

## Algorithm
1. Create a stack and initialize it as empty.
2. For the STL stack version, push elements onto the stack and remove the top element using pop.
3. For the linked-list version, insert nodes at the head and remove them from the head.
4. Check whether the stack is empty and display its contents when needed.

---

## How it works
A stack follows the LIFO (Last In, First Out) principle. The last inserted element is removed first. In the linked-list version, the head acts as the top of the stack.

---

## Functionality
- Push an element onto the stack
- Pop the top element
- Check whether the stack is empty
- Display the contents of the stack

---

## Time and Space Complexity
- Push / Pop: O(1)
- Display: O(n)
- Extra space: O(n) for the linked-list version and stack storage
